From 470329c2610bd052143215adf3531dbc3a5ec823 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jake Gaylor <jhgaylor@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 02:05:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(db): offer P-256 as the last-resort TLS group so stock
 PostgreSQL 17 servers can connect

The pool restricted CurvePreferences to X25519MLKEM768 and X25519. PostgreSQL
17 and earlier default ssl_ecdh_curve to prime256v1 alone, and managed
offerings such as CloudNativePG pin that parameter, so every TLS connect to a
stock server failed with 'tls: handshake failure' while psql (OpenSSL, offers
P-256) connected fine. Append CurveP256 after the X25519 groups: order is the
client preference and TLS 1.3 servers honour it, so a PQ-capable server still
negotiates the hybrid, and logNegotiatedCurve already reports anything below
X25519MLKEM768 as a downgrade event.

Reproduced and verified against CloudNativePG 1.29 / PostgreSQL 17.6: before,
init could apply the schema but keys publish and every write session failed;
after, publish/capture/search/doctor succeed with negotiated_curve=P-256 logged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 internal/db/pool.go | 16 ++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/internal/db/pool.go b/internal/db/pool.go
index de3847d..3d17ca4 100644
--- a/internal/db/pool.go
+++ b/internal/db/pool.go
@@ -162,14 +162,22 @@ func NewPool(ctx context.Context, cfg Config) (*Pool, error) {
 
 	p := &Pool{logger: logger}
 
-	// PQ-TLS (DESIGN §2). Prefer X25519MLKEM768, fall back to X25519.
-	// A downgrade to X25519 is an observability event, not an error.
-	// If the resolved URL has no TLS (e.g. sslmode=disable for the local
-	// default), TLSConfig is nil and we leave it alone.
+	// PQ-TLS (DESIGN §2). Prefer X25519MLKEM768, fall back to X25519, and
+	// keep P-256 as the last resort: PostgreSQL 17 and earlier default
+	// ssl_ecdh_curve to prime256v1 alone (and managed offerings such as
+	// CloudNativePG pin it), so a client offering only the X25519 groups
+	// cannot complete a handshake with a stock server at all ("tls:
+	// handshake failure" on every connect). Group ORDER is the client's
+	// preference and a TLS 1.3 server honours it, so a PQ-capable server
+	// still negotiates the hybrid; anything below X25519MLKEM768 is logged
+	// as a downgrade by logNegotiatedCurve. If the resolved URL has no TLS
+	// (e.g. sslmode=disable for the local default), TLSConfig is nil and
+	// we leave it alone.
 	if poolCfg.ConnConfig.TLSConfig != nil {
 		poolCfg.ConnConfig.TLSConfig.CurvePreferences = []tls.CurveID{
 			tls.X25519MLKEM768,
 			tls.X25519,
+			tls.CurveP256,
 		}
 	}
 
